    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Peter E. Kern founded the neighborhood in 1914, turning his ranch into a planned subdivision.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kern_Place"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1916 Kern built a wrought‑iron and stone archway at North Kansas and Robinson, costing $2,500, to mark the entrance to the community.",
